  "all_ingredients_flat": "brown rice flour, water, hing (asafoetida), roasted cumin powder, black pepper powder, amchoor (mango powder), saunf (fennel seeds) powder, date paste, sesame seeds, aquafaba, homemade Tomato Sauce, Mint Chutney, Date-Amla Chutney",
  "instructions": "Mix brown rice flour, saunf powder & roasted cumin powder in half of the water. Mix carefully. Avoid making any lumps. Boil the rest of the water. Pour the flour & spice mixture in it. Keep stirring for several minutes. Mixture combines like a ball, leaving the sides of pan.\nPour the mixture into a glass container lined with parchment paper. Sprinkle some sesame seeds, roasted cumin powder & mango powder. Refrigerate for 2-3 hours. Cut into pieces.\nServe with chutneys of your choice: homemade Tomato Sauce, Mint Chutney, Date-Amla Chutney.\nFor crispiness, coat with aquafaba and air fry.",
